' Question: what runs on the caller's thread when an alert is raised, and where does it stop?
' Explained by: ../05-building-blocks.md, which cites each component. Drawn by hand, high level.
' An arrow's label is the port it crosses; the box at its head implements it.
@startuml 05-publish-path
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction
[BotAlertSource] as S
[AlertHub] as H
[InMemoryAlertSettings] as SET
[SqliteOutbox] as O
S --> H : IAlertPublisher\npublish, condition_cleared
H --> SET : IAlertSettingsSource\ncurrent
H --> O : IOutbox\nenqueue (one transaction)
note bottom of H : inhibit, deduplicate, hold,\ngroup, route, admit;\nnever calls a channel
@enduml
